     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thursday, June 29, 2023 at 12:56:25 PM UTC+9 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jmals...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Kushaal,</div><div><br></div><div>Your individual.local.identifier should be the same across each individual. It looks like you imported the unique location ID in this column, so your telemetry object is only one row long.</div><div><br></div><div>Jesse<br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wed, Jun 28, 2023 at 8:45 PM Kushaal Selvarajah &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">kush...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>Thank you Jesse and Chris,</div><div><br></div><div>I have made progress! Your advice helped. However, I am running into a new problem. I keep getting the below error when I attempt to produce a variogram.<br></div><div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n<span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">vg.cilla&lt;-variogram(serow)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in rep(0, nrow(data)) : invalid &#39;times&#39; argument</span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><font style=\"font-family:Arial\" color=\"#000000\"><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\">Below is my current script and how my data frame looks like before converting into as.telemetry;</span></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"></span></span></font><br>df &lt;- read.csv(&quot;C:/Users/Kushaal/Downloads/serow_trial2a.csv&quot;<br>               , stringsAsFactors = FALSE)<br><br>df$timestamp &lt;- as.POSIXct(df$timestamp, tz = &quot;UTC&quot;, format = &quot;%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%OS&quot;)<br><br>serow &lt;- as.telemetry(df, timezone=&quot;UTC&quot;)<br><br>#Plotthepositions <br>plot(serow)<br><br>#Calculatevariogram <br>vg.serow&lt;-variogram(serow)</div><div><br></div><div><img alt=\"DF screenshot.png\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/ctmm-user/attach/1f8661046bdbb/DF%20screenshot.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" width=\"605px\" height=\"124px\"><br></div><div><br></div><div>Could there be an error still in my timestamp? Sorry I am fairly new to this field. <br></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thursday, June 29, 2023 at 3:13:23 AM UTC+9 <a rel=\"nofollow\">chris.h...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>Hi Kushaal,</div><div><br></div><div>You can try your luck with <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">timeformat=&quot;auto&quot;</span> or provide <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">timeformat</span> argument for the non-POSIX format that your timestamps are in: see <span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">help(&#39;as.telemetry&#39;)</span></div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Chris<br></div><div><br></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wednesday, June 28, 2023 at 5:25:20 AM UTC-4 Kushaal Selvarajah wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>Hi Chris,</div><div><br></div><div>I am currently using the ctmm package.<br></div><div>However, I keep running into the same error code and fail to find a solution. <br></div><div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n<span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">serow &lt;- as.telemetry(df, timezone=&quot;UTC&quot;)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in as.POSIXlt.character(x, tz, ...) : \r\n  character string is not in a standard unambiguous format</span></span></span></div><div><br>\r\n</div><div>Alternatively, is it possible to replicate our own data to that of Movebank format without having to upload it onto the site? <br></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you for your time. <br></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n-- <br></blockquote></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;ctmm R user group&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">ctmm-user+...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br></blockquote></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/ctmm-user/9ce0dfed-5ad9-43cc-ac8e-0f8546411078n%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=